# Phase 18 compatibility release gate — empty ProcessQueue commit parity
# Recorded: 2026-10-22 23:52:03 UTC
# Code revision: e1b8ffdb

## Compatibility finding

Pinned Java 5.5.1 `ProcessQueue.commit()` invokes
`consumingMsgOrderlyTreeMap.lastKey()` before mutating queue state. Calling it
without a preceding non-empty `takeMessages` therefore throws
`java.util.NoSuchElementException`; count, size, and the ready tree remain
unchanged. Rust now returns
`ProcessQueueError::EmptyOrderedConsumeSet` for this input instead of `-1`,
while successful commits return `Ok(offset)`.

The invoked `ConsumerFacadeApiFixtures` comparison includes the Java exception
class and the unchanged empty queue state. Fixture SHA-256:
`aa3a16d255ba6d331f5cb84e068db3b14e45f49c605671feebc97abc3aba8f81`.

